From 9fe356932d337bcb5328714143e51de901714760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:18:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: pacing holds are recorded skips; an idle
 account's null five_hour counts as a fresh window

Follow-ups to PR #3025 (LLM quota pacing governor), from exact-head review t_01a1dae9702e75d7
(pullrequestreview-5905947357). Card t_01a1dafcb027ff7b.

1. Paced holds read as "dispatcher skip reason unrecorded".
   A pacing hold appended `respawn_guarded` to the in-memory DispatchResult and wrote its own `llm_paced`
   event, but no `respawn_guarded` or `dispatch_skipped` event. `kanban_dispatch_skip._tick_skips` did not
   know the governor, so queue position, the chat-wait and parent-unclaimed notices said "skip reason
   unrecorded" after 30 min (and offered their generic advice), and `kanban diagnostics` called the card
   `stranded_in_ready`.
   Fix: the governor records `DispatchResult.llm_paced` (task, "<provider> <paced|held>, ...", until when
   held, per-provider state/limit/running). `_tick_skips` turns it into one `dispatch_skipped
   {reason: llm_paced}` row per episode. `words`/`advice` render "held: LLM quota pacing (anthropic paced
   pool)" plus "starts on its own once its provider pool is back on pace ... priority changes do not lift
   a pacing hold". Diagnostics read the episode's latest skip (`_episode_skip`, shared with the pinned
   quota wall) and report `held_in_ready` with hold_reason `llm_paced` (with the reset when held). A held
   skip whose reset has passed no longer counts as a hold. `llm_paced` is classified as a quiet-hold
   DispatchResult field.

2. An idle account added 0 sustainable rate.
   Live `/api/oauth/usage` (read-only, worker-4 pool, 2026-11-14T16:57Z; card comment 77613) returns
   `"five_hour": null` for 6 of 7 accounts: the whole window object, not `resets_at: null`.
   `account_usage` skips it, so those accounts had no five_hour reading. `_factor` summed sustainable rate
   only over headroom accounts with a reading and a reset. With account-secondary the only headroom account
   (7d 34%, 5h idle), account-primary's 5h burn made the five_hour factor 0, so the pool was PACED with limit 0
   while account-secondary was free.
   Fix: `_sustainable` counts a headroom account's missing window, or a window with no reset, as a fresh full
   window, `(target - used) / WINDOW_SECONDS[kind]`. Reserved accounts still add nothing.

3. Config and docs.
   `kanban.llm_pacing.*` is registered in config_defaults through the import-free
   `hermes_cli/kanban_pacing_defaults.py` (the pattern of `kanban_workspace_source_config`). A test pins it
   to `PacingConfig()`. The governor is documented in website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md (states,
   recorded skip, key table). File-line caps are offset in config_defaults (two joined default lines) and
   kanban_db_dispatch (one docstring as a comment).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_llm_pacing_followups.py (11).
RED on origin/main be9b942274 with only the test file: 9 failed, 1 passed (the reserved-account guard
already held; the config-registration test was added after the RED run). GREEN: 11/11.
Dispatch-level tests also cover the reviewer's surviving mutants:
- any->all: a class route with an ungoverned provider starts.
- class_providers=[]: a class:deep card is paced on its class's providers.
- local_running=0 and avg_running=0: avg 4 x factor 0.625 gives limit 2, so 2 of 3 cards start.
- is_deferrable=False: a priority -1 card gets floor(2 x 0.5) = 1 and waits behind the normal card.
scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
